From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:52:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 121/130] Go to line: Ctrl+G jumps to a line or line:column

Ctrl+G and Edit > Go to line... open a one-field bar where the find bar
sits. Enter moves the cursor to "42" or "42:7" (1-based), unfolds a fold
around the line as find hits do, scrolls it into view and gives the text
the focus back. Numbers past the end clamp to the last line or the end of
the line; anything else marks the field as an error and keeps it open.
Escape and the close button shut it, and it never shows together with the
find bar. goto_line::open() gives other places, such as a status bar, the
message that opens it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

